 "description": "<p>Kapisillit is a settlement in the Sermersooq municipality in southwestern Greenland. In 2010, the settlement had 86 inhabitants. Kapisillit means the salmon in the Greenlandic language. The name refers to the fact that the only spawning-ground for salmon in Greenland is a river near the settlement. Source: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kapisillit\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia</a></p><p>For further information (in Danish) see also the Danish Geodata Agency:&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.gronlandskehavnelods.dk/#HID=26\" target=\"_blank\">Den grønlandske Havnelods</a></p>",
